{"reference":"1 Samuel 5","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":5,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Ark Narrative","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Read this chapter within the ark narrative of 1 Samuel 4–6. Israel’s earlier treatment of the ark as a guarantee of victory is rejected: here, without an Israelite army, the LORD judges Dagon and the Philistine communities that hold the ark.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_005_3f1aced52de60e42767b00d9"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}